WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.770
The Q-Class were sent to the mountain mansion.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:48.480
of famous violinist Yugo Masaomi in order to investigate
a threatening letter from Hell’s Maestro.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.940
As the investigation proceeded, we became
suspicious of his four students.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:02:00.410
They had all been fighting over who would
their master’s prized violin, the Testa di Drago,

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:05.910
and had worked together to drive one
of them, Houshou Mitsuru, to suicide.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.380
One by one, they were killed at the mansion

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.340
and this tragedy was heading to an unimaginable climax.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.820
Kirishima-san!

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:44.450
A syringe?

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.080
Look!

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.750
As Honshou Mitsuru’s spirit ordered me,

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.540
I have executed the three sinners.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.840
The last of them is.me.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.760
Here then, I execute myself, and play
the final notes of this death concerto.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:03.510
Kirishima Sonata...

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.310
It looks like a suicide note.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.600
Then it was him who killed them?

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.560
We’re cursed.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.610
Every day we get calls, and at the other
end of the line is the sound of a violin:

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.030
Houshu Mitsuru’s “The Demon’s Banquet!”

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.750
To think that Kirishima-kun was the criminal.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.250
But that makes sense.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.170
He left the solo to prepare Shirase’s murder.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:44.100
But to think he would kill himself
after he had killed the others...

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.220
No. This isn’t over.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.230
I see

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:03.320
So the string of murders ended
up with the criminal’s suicide.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.530
What do you think, Kazuma?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.910
It doesn’t make any sense!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:08.990
'cause...

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:10.790
What?

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.000
Houshu Mitsuru’s?

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:12.960
What's wrong?

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.130
And they are in the mansion?

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.670
No way. He was Houshou-san’s...

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.130
That means...

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.050
He’s Hell’s Maestro!

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.640
No. It’s too early to say that.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.010
What do you think, Ryuu?

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:31.930
Ryuu.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.560
Sorry, I didn’t hear what you said.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.650
What's wrong, Ryuu?

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.150
No, nothing.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:43.200
What I don’t understand is how they killed Murasame.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.740
They didn’t know for certain that
he’d drink that whiskey, did they?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:55.460
Fukuoka-sensei said he was a rather obsessive-compulsive
person, and had a lot of habits, or obsessions rather.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:04.630
Like, he always ate alone, he always shook cans before
drinking them, he showered three times a day

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.430
and he always drank two glasses of whiskey after dinner.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.770
Could the criminal have used that information?

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:11.690
I get it!

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:16.020
If the criminal was a person who
knew Murasame-san’s habits,

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.980
it makes sense that they'd
put poison into the whiskey?

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:23.030
But isn’t that a little too improbable?

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:28.370
For one thing, after that murder, it’s possible that
he’d lose his: appetite and not take a drink.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.170
Mail from Kazuma!

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.290
Oh, I forgot!

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.420
Yes?

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.790
Don’t forget about me!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.380
I sent a you a question related to
the trick used in the poisoning.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.550
Umm...

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:52.100
If you throw a dice ten times, what is the probability that
you'll get a certain number more than once? What’s this?

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.020
99 9%

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.070
I see!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.480
I understand the trick the criminal used to in his murder!

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.150
Yeah.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.450
But with just that evidence it’s
difficult to identify the criminal.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:12.540
And we still haven’t uncovered everything with
regards to Shirase Mayumi’s murder alibi trick.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.620
That’s right.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:16.870
Kirishima should’ve been the only
one who could have done it.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.290
That’s not true.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:26.220
The criminal figured that his trick would be partially
uncovered, so he created another trick to hide it.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.680
Did you find the answer to that Kyuu?

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:31.190
Yes. I think I did.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.430
Alright!

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.930
Then let’s go get them!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.350
We can’t.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.350
Why?

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:44.940
If I’m right, anybody here could’ve killed her.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.360
This isn’t definitive either?

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:53.410
This is Kirishima’s. .

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.330
What's wrong, Kyuu?

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.250
I get it. That's it!

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:02.890
I get it!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.250
I get it!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.130
I've found the identity of Hell’s Maestro!

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:08.880
There’s three hints!

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.090
The first is the wooden floor.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.720
The second is the problem that
Kazuma sent about probabilities.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.560
The third is the violin case.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.980
And there’s one answer!

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:32.620
Oh my, Amakusa-kun, what are you doing here this late?

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.710
I knew it was you.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.130
Impressive indeed, Ryuu-sama.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.130
You did excellent work in locating me.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.050
Reliable as always.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.310
Is this all your doing?

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:01.270
I cannot say that to a DDS member.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.060
For the moment I am merely Shiba Asae, music collector.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.820
Not the criminal, just an observer.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:15.200
My, if I say any more, your grandfather
will be angry with me.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.620
We DDS have already solved the crime!

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:22.160
Once we have captured the criminal,
your turn will be next!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.800
I haven’t done anything, what are you going
* to turn me over to the police for?

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.170
Ryuu-sama, can I ask you one thing?

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.010
What?

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:40.060
Was it you who solved the crime?

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:42.850
Not me.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.810
I’m glad to hear that.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:48.270
I look forward to seeing your work.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.410
I’m sorry, Sir Anubis.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.080
Ryuu-sama has found me out.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:04.540
And it seems that DDS has uncovered our plans here.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:05.620
What?

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:07.330
But relax.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.630
It wasn’t Ryuu who solved all the murders.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:14.050
Then stay quiet and watch how things develop.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.140
Our plan was perfect.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:23.430
If there was a flaw in its execution, the
fault lies with the client, Hell’s Maestro.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:29.110
And what will eventually happen, even
DDS will not even be able to imagine.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.080
Sorry to keep you waiting, everyone.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.960
And I’m sorry to drag you out here,
especially when you’re tired.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.080
Hongou-san, what's going on?

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.790
You said you solved the crime.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:53.300
Didn’t it end with the criminal’s suicide?

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.800
I’m about to explain that.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.970
Now, begin, Q-Class!

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.390
This isn’t over yet.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.980
Both Kirishima-san’s suicide and suicide note were faked.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.980
The real criminal, Hell’s Maestro, Is
one of the people in this room!

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:18.780
This was a brilliantly executed plan intended
to make Kirishima look like the criminal.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:26.750
First of all, in order to make Kirishima lose his alibi, the
criminal sent those threatening phone calls to Kirishima.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.630
I heard it directly from

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:35.800
Those calls that he kept receiving, and “The
Banquet” that he heard at the other end;

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.590
when heard Yuge-sensei’s music
he couldn’t take it any more

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.350
and ran out of the room, thus losing his alibi.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.770
Just as the criminal wanted.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.640
Then the poison in the whiskey...

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.980
Yes. Kirishima-san didn’t do that either.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:56.440
The criminal knew that Murasame-san always drank
whiskey after dinner, and used that information.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:01.950
He couldn’t be certain of that; it’s too unreliable
to be used as a murder method.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:05.490
That’s the first hint: a question of probabilities.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:11.170
Another detective of ours who isn’t
here solved that problem for us.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:12.920
Here.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:14.710
Do you know what this is?

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:16.550
Salad dressing, right?

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:17.590
Yup!

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.970
But it’s got poison in it.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:23.550
But we used that too.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:24.640
That’s right.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.640
To be precise, the poison isn’t in it yet.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.610
If you shake this, the contents of the
capsule will dissolve in the liquid.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.610
Now that you mention it, Murasame-san had the habit of
eating or drinking only after shaking anything like that.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.700
That’s not all of it.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:49.960
All the other bottles in the kitchen had poison
set up like that dressing, and in the shower
in the annex baths, there was this.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:59.170
so he used the showers instead of the baths
because the hot water came out faster.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.720
The criminal knew that and put it there.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:07.350
But the criminal couldn’t be sure that any
of them would be successful, could he?

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:14.310
But even if one only had a 50% chance of success,
multiply it by an infinite number of times...

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:20.610
And the probability of success becomes
extremely close to 100%.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.320
Hey wait a minute!

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:26.740
He was the only one who didn’t have an
alibi when Shirase Mayumi was killed!

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.580
Amakusa-kun proved that!

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.710
That’s hint number two: the wooden floor.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:33.920
What?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.580
Look at this.

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:40.590
What?

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:43.220
Look at this wooden floor.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:48.640
The shock from the glass striking it and shattering
made a little scratch in the wooden floor, right?

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.980
Wooden floors are actually surprisingly soft,

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:55.270
and even something as little as this made a scratch in it.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:13:00.230
But in Shirase-san’s room there were no scratches at all.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:07.410
In other words, the criminal didn’t break the pots there,
he broke them elsewhere and brought them in.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:13.580
knowing in advance that the trick with the MD would
make  Kirishima lose his alibi,

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:17.040
and in the end made it look like he
committed suicide and killed him.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.590
But if both of them were executed
in an automated manner

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:24.260
then that means anybody in this
mansion could be a suspect!

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.590
You three DDS people too!

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:31.560
Making us think that itself is a psychological trick.

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:39.520
Sealed inside this mountain mansion, if a murder occurs, 
anybody would assume that the
criminal is somebody there.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:44.820
But that common sense itself is
the criminal’s greatest trick.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:46.490
Right?

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.310
You’re Hell’s Maestro!

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:56.860
Right?

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.200
You’re Hell’s Maestro!

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:00.410
Gotouda-san!

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:12.790
Even you, who wasn’t in the mansion.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:16.760
What nonsense!

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:22.550
If they were carried out in an automated manner,
but then what about Kirishima-kun?

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.100
4%
4.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:27.720
He was already dead by the time I got here!

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.190
I couldn’t have killed him.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:36.320
No, you had a chance to kill him.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:41.110
You had three reasons to seal off
the way here with dynamite.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:46.910
The first was, of course, to keep
the target in the mansion.

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:53.540
The second was to buy time for the automated
murder methods to kill Shirase and Murasame.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:59.050
And the third was to give yourself time to kill Kirishima.

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:04.890
You intended to kill Kirishima yourself, for whom you
plans to make it look like he killed himself.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.970
If all three were killed by automated methods,

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:11.140
somebody might have suspected that the
criminal was from outside the mansion,

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:14.900
because they needed to make the
conditions point towards suicide.

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:22.530
But you wanted all three murders committed before you
got here so that you could have the perfect alibi.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:25.280
So you used one more trick.

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:31.660
You screamed and made it sound
like somebody was falling.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.120
And then hid!

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:38.880
Then you snuck past Kinta and Hongou-sensei when they
went to look for you, and went into the mansion.

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:42.130
It was dark and the footing was bad;

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:45.550
it was 30 minutes after that they found you.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:49.770
What's wrong?

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:55.850
In those 30 minutes you killed him.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:16:02.400
made it look like a suicide, headed back to the cliff
and pretended you were passed out the whole time.

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:04.990
Right, Gotouda-san?!

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:08.700
I didn’t!

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:09.490
It’s not me!

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:10.700
Do you have proof?!

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.500
What you’re saying is just a hypothesis.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.250
Do you have any proof that I killed him?

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.340
The third hint: the violin case.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:23.630
Could you show us the violin you brought?

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:25.470
I've got it.

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:27.390
It won’t open though.

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:30.060
Well I uh... forgot the key.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:30.810
Touyama!

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:36.730
If somebody’s well-prepared despite not being a detective.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:39.650
Don’t you get it?

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:43.110
They would be the criminal!

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:47.820
This is...

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:55.290
Walking for what seems like an eternity in heavy rain,
even if your violin’s in a case it might damage easily.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:01.500
But if you knew that you had to walk that
far, and only bring an empty case,

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:04.760
that means that you premeditated the plan.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.840
Gotouda-kun.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:11.390
Gotouda-san, why didn’t you bring your violin?

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:18.520
If there was a murder, then of course you
wouldn’t be playing the violin at all.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:23.190
You knew that, so you didn’t bring it with you!

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.240
Am I wrong?

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:31.870
I thought about it until the very end.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:39.960
I couldn’t ruin my precious violin!

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:41.290
Gotouda-kun!

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.420
That means that you...

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:45.170
Yes

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.130
Sense, I did it.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:49.800
It was me.

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:54.770
I personally murdered the three who set up
that horrible trap for Houshou Mitsuru.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:56.310
No way!

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:59.480
Gotouda-san, you were not working together with them?

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:01.270
I didn’t know.

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:06.610
I merely thought that it would help her
out, so I scheduled a concert for her.

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:08.860
You can't have...

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:12.620
We loved each other.

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:21.040
Mitsuru was an irreplaceable person to
me, both as a lover and a violinist.

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:22.920
What?

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:24.540
An open concert?

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:27.590
But isn’t that the one you’re supposed to participate in?

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:32.260
What? I’m not giving it to you because I’m your lover.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:38.680
I'm giving it to you because I want to see 
the violinist I’m in love with perform
before the greatest critics in the world!

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:44.150
I want to prove that what I was hearing was right!

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.190
Manabu...

00:18:47.090 --> 00:18:51.110
But I never thought it would lead to tragedy.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:49.600
Waiting Room

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:49.600
Houshou Mitsuru

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:53.280
What?

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:54.120
Mitsuru has...

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:02.870
And she lost her fingers, her life as a violinist, to frostbite.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:07.010
After that, Mitsuru, who had been so bright and cheerful,

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:22.480
Mitsuru!

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:25.310
Wake up, Mitsuru!

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:31.530
Her cries of despair were left behind in her will

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:37.080
Of course, she had no idea that her cruel
fate had been deliberately planned.

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:44.460
But for some reason, her last note ended with this.

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:50.130
“Manabu, don’t let anybody have the Testa di Drago.

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:56.140
If you can, throw it into the sea, along with my body.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:00.220
Sensei’s violin is mine.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:02.810
I will hand it to no one.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:05.060
With death, I shall prove this.”

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:13.860
So this letter from Houshou Mitsuru wasn’t a
threatening letter, but was her last message.

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:17.070
Yes, that was the last page.

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:21.240
In order to determine the truth of the coincidences
which had driven her to her death,

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:27.790
I played “The Demon’s Banquet” to the other
three students each night over the phone.

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:33.220
That’s just one of Mitsuru’s fans or
something making a prank call!

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:37.930
If somebody found out that we set that trap for her...

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.510
We’re in big trouble!

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:40.720
Yeah!

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.730
But what we did made everything look like coincidence.

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:45.640
And she was the one who killed herself.

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:48.690
We haven’t done anything suspicious.

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:53.490
Even if she has come back from
Hell, she can’t do anything.

00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:00.580
Come back to life, Houshou Mitsuru!

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:02.040
Hell’s Maestro!

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:07.420
Bring death to those foul musicians
with a demonic melody!

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:12.250
No.

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:15.920
Tachiki, that’s...

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:21.390
I thought it was all four of you who had done it,

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:25.350
and was going to take revenge on
the last person who killed her.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.310
But I was wrong, wasn’t I?

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:31.360
You actually loved Mitsuru-neesan.

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:33.650
Mitsuru-neesan? You can’t mean...

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:35.820
Then Arisa-kun is...

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:36.650
Yes.

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:39.780
We've already made an inquiry into your background.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:45.750
They do have different names, but she is, without
a doubt, the younger sister of Houshou Mitsuru.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:00.550
But our plot isn’t over yet.

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:04.180
What is this pounding in my chest?

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:06.020
Something’s going to happen.

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:07.100
Something bad!

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:10.310
But you were gonna use a knife like this?

00:22:10.590 --> 00:22:11.190
Touyama!

00:22:15.300 --> 00:22:17.900
He who revealed the secrets of the gods,

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:19.860
Shall fall into Tartarus!

00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:23.280
Yes, kill the kid who found out our secret!

00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:43.220
What?

00:22:44.410 --> 00:22:45.010
Ryuu!

00:22:45.870 --> 00:22:47.810
He’s already going into shock from the loss of blood.

00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:50.190
Touyama, get my bag!

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:51.190
Yes!

00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:55.480
For now he’s stable.

00:22:55.710 --> 00:22:58.530
But he needs to be taken to a hospital immediately.

00:22:58.760 --> 00:23:00.860
Hongou-sensei, I'll go.

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:04.870
There may still be an unknown enemy here.

00:23:05.180 --> 00:23:07.950
You need to find out who they are,
in case anything else happens.

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:10.710
So I'll take Ryuu to the hospital myself

00:23:11.310 --> 00:23:12.580
Let me go, please!

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:18.130
Very well, but if you think the situation
becomes too difficult, just call for help.

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:18.880
Got it?

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:22.380
Hongou-san, let me go!

00:23:23.490 --> 00:23:24.850
Ryuu was only hurt because he shielded me!

00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:28.560
Didn't  you hear what Touyama said?

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.440
We still have things we have to do here!

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:37.150
Ryuu.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:47.070 --> 00:24:48.710
Kinta runs to a hospital to save Ryuu.

00:24:47.400 --> 00:24:56.100
Next Episode

00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:51.170
In front of him stands an unforeseen threat!

00:24:51.910 --> 00:24:54.300
Who is it that appears as their lives are at risk?

00:24:55.080 --> 00:24:58.680
Meanwhile, a brilliant psychological war takes
place at the mansion between DDS and Pluto.

00:24:59.500 --> 00:25:02.560
Will DDS be able to play the melody of hope in the end?

00:25:03.450 --> 00:25:04.900
Don't die Ryuu!

00:25:08.880 --> 00:25:12.700
This is the only thing to eat after work is done.

00:25:13.140 --> 00:25:15.320
If they find me I'll get yelled at,
so I’m sneakily eating this.

00:25:17.260 --> 00:25:18.490
Aah, Kazuma-sama!

00:25:18.960 --> 00:25:20.420
You're eating that junk food again?
